  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-03T01:22:33.972Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Your FAQ mentions that VRChat already holds claimed Date of Birth data for it's users through a question asked during terms of service agreement.\n\nIn my country (Australia) it is possible to revise birth records. While white folk tend to have births registered fairly promptly and fairly accurate dates, Indigenous people and immigrants without a valid visa often do not register births until much later, with Indigenous people sometimes deferring until adulthood when it becomes necessary to register to exist in a legal way in the coloniser government systems in order to do things like legally work. Because of this, sometimes birth records get updated later when more accurate information is found.\n\nHandling DOB information, you cannot safely assume that a DOB wont change over time. Ages can advance or regress suddenly by months or even years in situations like above. Additionally, users might fabricate false DOB inputs to avoid having you store real identity information in case of leaks and due to concerns of data brokers.\n\nHow will VRChat handle these situations, where ID DOB doesn't match TOS DOB data? Will VRChat have a formal process for people whose DOB has changed legally to update their records?",
